# Project Structure
- Next.js 15+ app router structure with authenticated and unauthenticated layouts
- TypeScript for type safety with strict type checking
- TailwindCSS with DaisyUI v5 for styling (business theme default)
- Prisma with PostgreSQL for database operations
- React Query for data fetching and caching
- Yours Wallet for BSV interactions

# API and Data Handling
- All API routes in app/api with proper auth middleware
- Use proper error handling with try/catch and typed responses
- Convert BigInt to string in API responses (especially for token amounts)
- Status endpoint is source of truth for system state and supply calculation
- Supply calculation must use mints/burns from status response
- Proper decimal handling using getConfig() for MNEE amounts
- Consistent date formatting across all tables

# Component Guidelines
- Components in src/components organized by type (charts, modals, pages)
- Pages in src/components/pages/dash/content
- Shared utilities in src/lib and src/utils
- Use 'use client' directive for interactive components
- Maintain mobile responsiveness with proper padding and grid layouts
- Prefer server components unless client interactivity needed

# State Management
- Global providers in app/providers.tsx:
  - ThemeContext for DaisyUI theme management
  - SystemStatusContext for pause state
  - BalanceContext for MNEE balances
  - QueryClient for React Query
  - YoursProvider for wallet integration
- Keep toast notifications in root layout with consistent styling
- Use React Query for server state management

# UI/UX Preferences
- Consistent table styling with status-based row coloring
- Clickable addresses with WhatsOnChain links and tooltips
- Compact button designs with text labels next to icons
- Loading states that preserve layout (especially charts)
- Modal close on outside click
- Input validation for decimal places based on token config
- K/M notation for large numbers in charts and tables
- Clear status indicators with action-oriented text

# Authentication
- NextAuth.js with email/password strategy
- Maintain auth checks in API routes and middleware
- Handle admin vs regular user permissions
- Proper session management in authenticated layout

# Code Style
- Use TypeScript interfaces over types
- Avoid any types - define proper interfaces
- Proper null checking and error handling
- Consistent naming (blacklist not block, freeze not pause)
- Keep components focused and modular
- Use descriptive variable names

# Data Models
- Proper relations between User, Customer, and Request models
- Status tracking with ActionStatus enum
- Consistent timestamp handling (createdAt, updatedAt)
- BigInt for token amounts
- Proper indexing on frequently queried fields

# Performance
- Implement proper polling intervals with React Query
- Optimize re-renders with proper dependency arrays
- Handle loading states gracefully
- Proper error boundaries and fallbacks